Regional Market Dynamics
The global natural food market demonstrates distinct regional characteristics:
•	North America: Dominates global consumption, supported by well-established organic certification systems and premium health food retail channels
•	Europe: Mature market with sophisticated consumer demand, particularly in Western European nations
•	Asia-Pacific: Fastest-growing region, driven by rapid urbanization and growing health awareness in China and India
•	Latin America: Emerging production hub for organic commodities serving global markets
•	Middle East & Africa: Nascent but promising market with increasing interest in imported natural food products
